2145	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"242e0e88","text":"Resolution of the daemon review of 2026-10-11 (block: 0 HIGH, 20 MED, 17 LOW), made after that review and not re-reviewed. CORRECTED in the definition (4): (1) languages: SQL files are already indexed, as one whole-file document (src/indexer/parser/artifact.ts), so the problem, FR012 and Story s9 now say SQL moves from a whole document to its structure, and the summary no longer says \"four more languages\"; (2) the assumption on reindexFile: it also removes the relationships of the entities it replaces (detachDeleteEntitiesInTxn, src/db/entities.ts) and does not write new relationships or touch the unresolved queue; (3) k9 names the local model as the tier named cheap, served by Ollama by default (docs/daemon.md:382); (4) the file-event check is at src/indexer/index.ts:766 and the watcher is src/indexer/watcher.ts, not src/daemon/watcher.ts (the definition cites neither path wrongly; noted for the design stage). VERIFIED BY HAND (16), each left unfinished by the review because its searches stop at 50 matches: reindexFile has no caller outside src/db/entities.ts:363; a reindex skips a file whose stored hash is unchanged unless cleanFirst (src/indexer/index.ts:1004-1008); the quoted sentences of ISSUE-12f70133 (root cause 1, reproduction steps 1-2, the re-export gap) and of ISSUE-61045de9 are in those files; ISSUE-0d577569 carries approvedAt 2026-10-10T12:01:29.521Z; CLAUDE.md:122 and :135 hold the two quoted rules; the non-git walker (walkFilesLegacy) filters by the name list only; RelationKind has no member the indexer emits between documents (REFERENCES is declared and never emitted under src/indexer); the Story dependency edges and the constraint ids were checked by the define checklist step. NOT read by hand: the body of the daemon shutdown path (finding on s4) and the migration-on-open code (finding on k5); both rest on the filed issues and are for the design stage to confirm.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:34:54.178Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
1166	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"91ae3dca","text":"Amended after approval, on the stakeholder's decisions of 2026-10-11 made while the high-level design was reviewed. (1) k11 and Story s6: the filter honours all three of git's ignore sources (.gitignore files, the clone's exclude file, the global ignore file); a file git tracks is indexed even when a rule matches; two built-in exclusions apply everywhere (generated or minified files, the daemon's own .insrc directory); a plain folder is filtered by the rules alone (ac9 reworded). (2) Story s1: the pickScope figure is removed from ac2 because that function no longer exists in the source, and the Story's design names the re-export case instead; ac4 says completeness is a field shown beside the status, whose four values are kept. (3) Story s7 ac2: an ambiguous call stays pending with its candidates and is reported apart; the value \"chosen among candidates\" is reserved. These amendments were not re-reviewed as a definition.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:31:05.256Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
669	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"49db72d4","text":"Amended after approval, 2026-10-11, on the stakeholder's decision: reindex is the one command and indexes every file from scratch, whether or not its content has changed; there is no separate repair. Today repo.reindex skips every file whose stored content hash is unchanged (src/indexer/index.ts:628 and :1004-1008). Not re-reviewed. Open for the stakeholder to confirm: unchanged text with an unchanged embedding model keeps its vector.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:43:12.977Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
527	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"8f6d646b","text":"Clarified by the stakeholder, 2026-10-11: a reindex calls the delete operations on the graph store and the vector store for the repository and builds everything again, vectors and document summaries included. This supersedes the earlier note that unchanged text keeps its vector. Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:46:08.673Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
565	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"665b06ab","text":"Amended after approval, 2026-10-11, on the stakeholder's decision: while a repository is being indexed or reindexed, search and analyze requests about it return a named error that states the indexing state, and no partial answer. Carried by Story s5 (a new requirement and acceptance criterion ac4 in the definition). Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:53:00.814Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
503	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"dd70abc7","text":"Stakeholder decision, 2026-10-11: a reindex is queued at once, for a request and for the migration alike; only the repository being reindexed is offline, from the start of its own run until that run completes, and other repositories are answered as usual. Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:56:39.209Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
722	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"1ee8d3e4","text":"Amended after approval, 2026-10-11, on the stakeholder's decision: Story s4 is reworded to the cause reproduced that day. The failure is not the semaphore limit: the daemon loses its file lock on the lock file when another descriptor on it is closed in-process, and another process that opens and closes the store then removes the semaphores. The title, the first and third criteria and the first requirement of s4 now speak of the store not being broken by another process. Not re-reviewed.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:16:16.230Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
499	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"6a590cf7","text":"Stakeholder decision, 2026-10-11: the temporary allowance that lets the MCP server open the live store until Story s11 is kept, and its removal is a required part of Story s11 (a new acceptance criterion ac6, requirement and local constraint on s11 in the definition).","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T09:27:55.689Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
728	{"artifactId":"DEF-c2ba6fa62a148ed1","entry":{"id":"86c392af","text":"Amended 2026-10-12 by the stakeholder's decision at the start of the plan for Story s11: s11 gains acceptance criterion ac7, that only the daemon opens the live vector store (~/.insrc/lance) and any other process is refused before the directory is created or connected. It records decision D4 of the s11 design (the vector store gets the owner rule Story s4 gave the graph store), which went beyond s11's six criteria; the stakeholder chose to amend the definition now rather than after the build.","actor":{"id":"legacy:subho-ghosh","kind":"person","properties":{"name":"Subho Ghosh"}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T11:20:36.148Z","feedback":[],"kind":"comment"}}
